    "Paragraph 1 sets out two stories and says 'Neither is quite right'. Paragraph 2 rejects the first (outrage is old), paragraphs 3 and 4 reject the second (reaction is not endorsement; the feed 'shapes the supply'), and paragraph 5 qualifies any remedy. The correct answer states that double rejection and the author's alternative.",
    "Choosing one of the two stories the passage reports and rejects.",
